<title>POLAND: Polish trade gap up at $982 mln Jan - stats office.</title>
<headline>Polish trade gap up at $982 mln Jan - stats office.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's registered trade gap in January was $982 million, 31.4 percent more than in January 1996, the Central Statistical Office said (GUS).  </p>
<p> POLISH TRADE		   JANUARY 1997	 JANUARY 1996</p>
<p> Trade balance			-981.6		  -747.2</p>
<p> exports			     2,138.1		 1,912.4</p>
<p> imports			     3,119.7		 2,659.6</p>
<p> TRADE WITH EU		  JANUARY 1997	 JANUARY 1996</p>
<p> Trade balance			-418.8		  -353.5</p>
<p> exports			     1,581.9		 1,324.9</p>
<p> imports			     2,000.7		 1,678.4</p>
<p>NOTE - GUS trade data differs from data reported by the National Bank of Poland (central bank) because GUS bases its figures on customs receipts while the NBP reports cash flows. -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
